{%- comment -%}
  Fyxx: Rewards band (product block)
  Part of the wine-template buy column, directly under the buy buttons.
  Shows the money value the bottle earns back in LoyaltyLion points, the only
  figure that comes straight from the earn rule.

  Earn rule: points = floor((variant price in JD, VAT stripped) x tier rate).
  Prices are tax-inclusive and points are awarded on the subtotal only, so the
  base is price / vat_divisor (a block setting defaulting to 1.16 for Jordan's
  16% VAT, so a rate change is an admin edit, not a code one). Floor, not round,
  because the band is a promise and must never state more than the customer
  receives. Tier rates: Blue 3, Silver 4, Gold 5, Platinum 5. variant.price is
  in fils, so divide by 100 first. 100 points = 1 JD across the fixed-amount
  rewards, so jd = points / 100, to two decimals.

  Two states, held at the same height so the card never shrinks on login:
    Signed out: two lines, no chip. Line 1 is the Blue-rate value with "from"
      (Blue is the lowest of four rates); line 2 is "Sign in to see your rate"
      with "Sign in" linking to login (carrying ?return_url back to the product).
    Signed in: one line, vertically centred, with a tier chip on the right. The
      figure is the member's own tier rate, with no "from". Line 2 is dropped:
      the chip and the personalised figure already carry what it said.
  Both states are pinned to the signed-out height with min-height plus
  align-items: center, so the signed-in single line centres in the same box
  rather than the card collapsing.

  Exclusion: LoyaltyLion zeroes the rate for anything in the collection
  "ll-fyxx-rewards-exclude". On those products this renders nothing at all.

  No tier colours: every tier shows the same blush band and the same ink chip.
  The tier is named in the chip, not painted. The old tier gradients, including
  the Platinum one, are gone.

  No JavaScript: the value reflects the first/selected variant at page load and
  does not recalculate when the variant changes. No font-family is declared; the
  lockup uses the theme heading font via its token.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign excluded = false
  for c in product.collections
    if c.handle == 'll-fyxx-rewards-exclude'
      assign excluded = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- unless excluded -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign price_jd = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | divided_by: 100.0
    assign vat_divisor = block.settings.vat_divisor | default: '1.16' | plus: 0
    if vat_divisor <= 0
      assign vat_divisor = 1.16
    endif
    assign base_jd = price_jd | divided_by: vat_divisor

    assign tier = ''
    if customer
      assign tier = customer.metafields.loyaltylion.loyalty_tier
    endif

    assign rate = 3
    case tier
      when 'Silver'
        assign rate = 4
      when 'Gold'
        assign rate = 5
      when 'Platinum'
        assign rate = 5
    endcase

    assign points = base_jd | times: rate | floor
    assign jd_whole = points | divided_by: 100.0 | floor
    assign jd_hundreds = jd_whole | times: 100
    assign jd_cents = points | minus: jd_hundreds
    assign jd_cents_padded = jd_cents | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2

    assign signed_in = false
    if customer and tier != blank
      assign signed_in = true
    endif
  -%}

  <div class="fx-rewards" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <div class="fx-rewards__lockup" role="img" aria-label="Fyxx Rewards">
      <span class="fx-rewards__mark">fyxx</span>
      <span class="fx-rewards__word">Rewards</span>
    </div>

    <span class="fx-rewards__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="fx-rewards__text{% if signed_in %} fx-rewards__text--solo{% endif %}">
      <p class="fx-rewards__points">Earn {% unless customer %}from {% endunless %}{{ jd_whole }}.{{ jd_cents_padded }} JD back on this bottle</p>
      {%- unless signed_in -%}
        <p class="fx-rewards__signin"><a href="{{ routes.account_login_url }}?return_url={{ product.url }}">Sign in</a> to see your rate</p>
      {%- endunless -%}
    </div>

    {%- if signed_in -%}
      <span class="fx-rewards__chip">{{ tier }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <style>
    .fx-rewards {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 18px;
      min-height: 78px;
      box-sizing: border-box;
      padding: 16px 20px;
      margin: 4px 0;
      background: #F8D3D7;
      border-radius: 4px;
      color: #100F0D;
    }
    .fx-rewards__lockup {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      line-height: 1;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
    }
    .fx-rewards__mark {
      font-family: var(--element-text-font-family--heading), var(--element-text-font-family-fallback--heading);
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: 19px;
      color: #100F0D;
    }
    .fx-rewards__word {
      margin-top: 2px;
      font-size: 9px;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: #100F0D;
    }
    .fx-rewards__divider {
      align-self: stretch;
      flex: 0 0 1px;
      width: 1px;
      background: rgba(16, 15, 13, 0.22);
    }
    .fx-rewards__text {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      min-width: 0;
    }
    /* Signed in drops line 2, so give its vertical footprint back to the text
       column, split evenly above and below, so the band holds the signed-out
       height and the single line centres in it rather than the card shrinking
       on login. The value is line 2's own margin plus line box, halved. */
    .fx-rewards__text--solo {
      padding-block: calc((3px + 12.5px * 1.3) / 2);
    }
    .fx-rewards__points {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 15px;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.3;
      color: #100F0D;
    }
    .fx-rewards__signin {
      margin: 3px 0 0;
      font-size: 12.5px;
      line-height: 1.3;
      color: rgba(16, 15, 13, 0.7);
    }
    .fx-rewards__signin a {
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 2px;
    }
    .fx-rewards__chip {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      margin-left: auto;
      font-size: 9.5px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #ffffff;
      background: #100F0D;
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 5px 11px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  </style>
{%- endunless -%}
